#{[17592186359833 #edb/ref 1080 "0.13" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186359833 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186359833 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ea0097db-0220-5610-aa9c-bf8496bfb7cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186359876 #edb/ref 1080 "0.23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186359876 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186359876 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ee51d506-3a45-567d-86d2-6491d5d72676" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360193 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186357894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360193 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186358408 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360193 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186358525 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360193 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186359833 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360193 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186359876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360193 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360193 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360193 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186358525 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360193 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "79790386-5ca3-5b7e-a326-b45ba6bd2fed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360541 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360541 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95024" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360541 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360541 #edb/ref 1071 "The time that a particular laptop battery lasts is normally distributed with a mean of $32$ hours and a standard deviation of $4$ hours. What is the probability that a full charge lasts for $36$ hours or more? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8159\\,$ | $\\,0.8186\\,$ | $\\,0.8212\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.8413\\,$ | $\\,0.8438\\,$ | $\\,0.8461\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.8643\\,$ | $\\,0.8665\\,$ | $\\,0.8686\\,$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360541 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5563fda7-bd6a-55bd-869b-0a5d94077bb5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360541 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $X$ represent the time the full charge lasts. Then we have $X∼N(32,{4}^{2}).$\n\nWe want to find $P(X\\ge 36).$ Thus, we convert $X$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 36) & =P(Z\\ge \\frac{36-32}{4}) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge 1) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le 1) \\\\  & =1-Φ(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\n1-Φ(1)=1-0.8413≈0.1587.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a full charge lasts $36$ hours or more is approximately $0.16.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361045 #edb/ref 1080 "images/cd/cd1f754fa00d1af2d8901ecc4c0cac434afb433474685fe7777d74f1703bafb2.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361045 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361045 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2eeddbc3-0c2b-51c9-a0c9-e864cef13cda" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361085 #edb/ref 1080 "I and IV only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361085 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361085 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "36b8832f-f459-53a5-bebf-7fce914129df" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361108 #edb/ref 1080 "images/c5/c5e335ffe5f2343671d1f9eca6cedc34ef34a9700837451e963cfcfe1cd153d5.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361108 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361108 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3b5a1453-83df-5991-9fd6-135cf92a1272" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361122 #edb/ref 1080 "images/eb/eb621888b04d5bd9b842624c278422995db44097adde61bbc769e8df0a5a47e7.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361122 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361122 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3f0f0bcd-a732-5