2\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 6 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=-\\frac{3}{2},$ $c=\\frac{3}{2},$ and $\\frac{a}{c}=\\frac{(-\\frac{3}{2})}{(\\frac{3}{2})}=-1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366133 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366134 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366133 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366133 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366136 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366133 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366137 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366133 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366138 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366133 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366133 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366133 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186366138 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366133 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "22bd81a8-fc97-5b1d-aab5-22729b731045" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366134 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{3}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366134 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366134 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "162d9cfd-034a-5c33-9d0a-906cac7f6fc2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366135 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366135 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366135 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a0e94b1d-482a-5d97-a07a-fd91a8e31af6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366136 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366136 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366136 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5e6ee2b1-5486-5bb5-8122-ecb889f89cb4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366137 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366137 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366137 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "09cba4a0-9f24-50ca-aaaf-b5d7a53af3e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366138 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366138 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366138 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ca0db238-7843-5a87-bfad-905b7e4e7ee9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371555 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186371556 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371555 #edb/ref 1069 "q-109326" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371555 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371555 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the arc of the curve $x=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{12}+\\frac{1}{y}$ that lies between the lines $y=1$ and $y=e.$ Calculate the surface area generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371555 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "59c768e0-123a-5f86-b9a6-1b397e77b597" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371555 #edb/ref 1074 "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi y\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $x=f(y),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nWe are told that the limits of integration are from ${y}_{1}=1$ to ${y}_{2}=e.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{{y}^{3}}{12}+\\frac{1}{y})=\\frac{{y}^{4}-4}{4{y}^{2}}\\,⇒\\,{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}=\\frac{{y}^{8}-8{y}^{4}+16}{16{y}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}y\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{y}^{8}-8{y}^{4}+16}{16{y}^{4}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}y\\sqrt{\\frac{{y}^{8}+8{y}^{4}+16}{16{y}^{4}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}\\,y\\sqrt{\\frac{({y}^{4}+4)^{2}}{16{y}^{4}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}y(\\frac{{y}^{4}+4}{4{y}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{y}^{4}+4}{y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}{\\int }_{1}^{e}({y}^{3}+\\frac{4}{y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}{(\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)\\,|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}(\\frac{{e}^{4}}{4}+4-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{8}({e}^{4}+15).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371556 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371557 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371556 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371558 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371556 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371559 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371556 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371560 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371556 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371561 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371556 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371556 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371556 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186371560 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371556 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cfb25814-53f0-5252-8e81-2248d22b22d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371557 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\pi }{15}({e}^{4}+1)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371557 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371557 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e775560f-3f4c-54be-841d-b0c3d21fd878" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371558 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{4\\pi }{15}({e}^{4}-12)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371558 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371558 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "32562cc2-5b04-5833-b156-51f71e7dd7ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371559 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\pi {e}^{2}}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371559 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371559 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "deec031c-a589-562b-a505-50630bb393d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371560 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\pi }{8}({e}^{4}+15)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371560 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371560 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5fd98cc9-8e2e-5c55-8146-376a748259e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371561 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\pi {e}^{4}}{32}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371561 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371561 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4d694888-90d9-5e06-bcb4-c0145a723e0c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371865 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186371866 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371865 #edb/ref 1069 "q-149725" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371865 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371865 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}3{a}_{i}(4-{b}_{j})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}=30,\\,{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}{b}_{j}=45.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371865 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9cefe9ad-c8c4-50df-9dcf-62888d4bac69" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371865 #edb/ref 1074 "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{b}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}3{a}_{i}(4-{b}_{j}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}3{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}(4-{b}_{j}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}3{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}(4-{b}_{j}) & =(3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i})\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}4-{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}{b}_{j}) \\\\  & =(3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i})\\cdot (4{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}1-{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}{b}_{j}) \\\\  & =(3\\cdot 30)\\cdot (4\\cdot 12-45) \\\\  & =(90)\\cdot (48-45) \\\\  & =(90)\\cdot (3) \\\\  & =270\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175