2186371942 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371944 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371942 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371945 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371942 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371946 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371942 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371947 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371942 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371942 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371942 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186371947 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371942 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "83cff6c6-9176-54ce-9248-48c8a44d7c5a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371943 #edb/ref 1080 "\\pi {\\int }_{-1}^{1}(1+{z}^{4})\\sqrt{1+8{z}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}z" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371943 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371943 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "19fd857a-69bb-52bc-8fb2-b57c6fb65bf8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371944 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\pi {\\int }_{-1}^{1}(1+{z}^{4})\\sqrt{1+8{z}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}z" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371944 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371944 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1146da46-595d-55c2-874f-d7177d74a0a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371945 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\pi {\\int }_{-1}^{1}(1+{z}^{4})\\sqrt{1+16{z}^{8}}\\,\\text{d}z" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371945 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371945 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fc506864-2f86-51e9-b176-0329e981f791" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371946 #edb/ref 1080 "\\pi {\\int }_{-1}^{1}(1+{z}^{4})\\sqrt{1+16{z}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}z" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371946 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371946 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "82ddc8e9-2ce1-5932-875c-df7ef67f9b63" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371947 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\pi {\\int }_{-1}^{1}(1+{z}^{4})\\sqrt{1+16{z}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}z" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371947 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371947 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "67776efe-de42-57c3-8ff4-ba76605d7146" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371948 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186371949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371948 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161098" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371948 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371948 #edb/ref 1071 "Use a fundamental vector product to determine which of the following integrals gives the surface area generated when the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡z$ is rotated by $2\\pi $ radians about the $z$-axis for $z\\in [1,e].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371948 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1297d2b2-529f-5b54-8024-028cb62e9052" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371948 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡z\\ge 0$ for all $z\\in [1,e].$ The parametrization of our surface of revolution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=⟨f(z)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,f(z)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z⟩,\\,(z,\\theta )\\in D\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡z,$ and\n\n$$\nD={(z,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le z\\le e,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{z}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂z},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂z},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂z}⟩=⟨{f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,{f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{\\theta }^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta },\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta },\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂\\theta }⟩=⟨-f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,f(y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{z}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ {f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & {f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & 1 \\\\ -f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & 1 \\\\ f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & 1 \\\\ -f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & {f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ -f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,{f}^{′}f{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{f}^{′}f{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,{f}^{′}f⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{z}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′}‖ & =\\sqrt{(-f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(-f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+({f}^{′}f)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{f}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )+{f}^{2}({f}^{′})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{f}^{2}+{f}^{2}({f}^{′})^{2}} \\\\  & =f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{z}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′}‖\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}\\cdot \\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f=\\operatorname{ln}⁡z,$ we obtain ${f}^{′}=\\frac{1}{z}.$ So, finally, we conclude that our expression for the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡z\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{1}{z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡z\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371949 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371949 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 